# d3drec op table: the ONE definition of every record in a .d3dr log.
# gen_ops.py turns it into src/ops_gen.h (C++ recorder) and ops.js (JS reader). Edit here, then run gen_ops.py.
#
# <code> <Interface>::<Method> <sig>
# code: 0..96 IDirect3DDevice8 vtable index | 100+ IDirect3D8 | 120+ IDirect3DTexture8 | 140+ IDirect3DSurface8
#       152+ IDirect3DVertexBuffer8 | 166+ IDirect3DIndexBuffer8 | 192+ meta records | 240 HR prefix
# Interface records (code < 192) start with the varuint id of `this`; meta records do not.
# sig (fields after `this`, in order; '-' = no fields):
#   u varuint32          i zigzag varint32       d raw u32 (4 bytes LE)   f raw f32
#   o object id (varuint, 0 = NULL / not a wrapped object)
#   r optional RECT (u8 0|1, then 4 x i)          R RECT/D3DRECT list (varuint n+1, 0 = NULL; then n x 4 i)
#   P POINT list (varuint n+1, 0 = NULL; then n x 2 i)
#   M matrix through a 4096-slot cache shared by all M fields: u8 0 = NULL | 1 = new (16 x f32; stored in slot
#     (newCount++ & 4095)) | 2 = cached (varuint slot)
#   B bytes (varuint len+1, 0 = NULL; then len bytes)   s string (same as B, UTF-8)
#   X lock data: u8 kind: 0 none | 1 NEW (u blobId, u len, bytes) | 2 REF (u blobId) | 3 DIFF (u nSpans, nSpans x (u skip, u len, bytes))
#     (DIFF spans are relative to the locked range; skip counts from the end of the previous span; DrawPrimitiveUP /
#     DrawIndexedPrimitiveUP vertex and index data use X too, so text/fog quads repeated every frame cost a REF)

